## Why Tools Over Prompt Injection

1. **Intentional Memory Access** - The agent consciously decides when to "remember"
2. **Transparent Process** - Users see when memory is being queried
3. **Error Handling** - Can gracefully handle memory failures
4. **Lacanian Timing** - Memory references become part of the interpretive act
5. **Ethical Bracketing** - Clear separation between conversation and memory systems

This architecture leverages the new LangChain v1's focus on agents while maintaining the philosophical integrity you're seeking. The tool-based approach actually aligns better with Lacanian practice - the "interpreter" consciously decides when to bring the past into the present.

